<del></del></span> Recommended Gear for Fury Warriors in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="what-is-the-bis-fury-warrior-gear">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="$color" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_questionmark.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> What is the BiS Fury Warrior gear?</h3>With many different sources of gearing and loot scarcity in Mists of Pandaria Classic, targeting your absolute Best in Slot gear isn't always realistic; so we've created a Best in Slot guide with all the ideal Fury Warrior drops found from raids, dungeons, Reputation, and World Bosses to help you decide what to prioritize.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>In Phase 3, a lot of the best items drop from the final boss, <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=69473/ra-den">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ra-den</span></a>. This boss is only progressable once you have killed all the previous bosses on the heroic Difficulty. Therefore, it may not be applicable for everyone to aim for a BiS setup including Ra-Den loot. If this is the case for you, it's a great idea to reference the <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/classes/warrior/arms/dps-stat-priority-pve">Stat Priorities for Fury Warriors</a> to help determine your own BiS based on what gear is available to you.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<br/>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="bis-gear">Overall Best in Slot Gear for Fury Warriors</h3>This list represents the best gear currently available for Fury Warriors, all of which is obtained from the raid, Throne of Thunder. This list excludes as much Thunderforged gear as possible. But to be clear, Thunderforged gear and normal Heroic Loot are just as powerful, both capping out at 541 item-level. The only benefit of Thunderforged loot is that it saves you some Justice Points, since you don't have to upgrade it.<br/>
